#metadata(title = "Mote Inline Code Font", author = "Mote")

#document(
  page = { size = "letter" },
  margin = { top = pt(54), right = pt(72), bottom = pt(54), left = pt(72) }
)

#font(
  name = "mono",
  latin = "Andale Mono",
  files = {
    regular = "/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Andale Mono.ttf",
    bold = "/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Andale Mono.ttf",
    italic = "/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Andale Mono.ttf",
    bold_italic = "/System/Library/Fonts/Supplemental/Andale Mono.ttf"
  }
)

#style(
  name = "Normal",
  type = "paragraph",
  run = { size = pt(11), color = "#111827" },
  paragraph = {
    spacing = {
      after = pt(9),
      line = { rule = "multiple", value = 1.12 }
    }
  }
)

#style(
  name = "CodeBase",
  type = "character",
  run = { font = "mono", size = pt(10.5), bold = true }
)

#style(
  name = "Code",
  type = "character",
  based_on = "code base",
  run = { color = "#7c3aed", bold = false }
)

#style(
  name = "CodeAccent",
  type = "character",
  based_on = "CodeBase",
  run = { size = pt(12), color = "#047857", bold = true }
)

# Inline Code Font

DOCX, PDF, and PNG should use the declared character style and Andale Mono face for ordinary markdown code instead of silently substituting a backend-specific Courier fallback.

## Implicit Inherited Code Style

The four samples below must have identical glyph shapes, character widths, regular weight, size, and purple color. `Code` inherits its font and size from `CodeBase`, explicitly disables the base bold setting, and the nested outer span must not override those character-style properties.

#table(
  width = inch(6.5),
  layout = "fixed",
  alignment = "center",
  cell = {
    margin = { all = pt(8) },
    borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#94a3b8" } }
  }
)[
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Reference span**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[#span(style = "Code")[iiii WWWW 0000 abcd 1234]]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Markdown backticks**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[`iiii WWWW 0000 abcd 1234`]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Code directive**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[#code(style = "Code")[iiii WWWW 0000 abcd 1234]]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Nested outer span**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[#span(font = "Times", size = pt(16), color = "#dc2626")[`iiii WWWW 0000 abcd 1234`]]
  ]
]

## Explicit Alternate Style

An explicit derived character style must replace the implicit Code style instead of being overwritten afterward. These two green samples must match one another and retain the monospace face inherited from `CodeBase`.

#table(
  width = inch(6.5),
  layout = "fixed",
  alignment = "center",
  cell = {
    margin = { all = pt(8) },
    borders = { all = { style = "single", size = 6, color = "#94a3b8" } }
  }
)[
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Reference span**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[#span(style = "CodeAccent")[alpha beta 42]]
  ]
  #row[
    #cell(width = inch(1.65), fill = "#f8fafc")[**Styled code**]
    #cell(width = inch(4.85))[#code(style = "CodeAccent")[alpha beta 42]]
  ]
]

The surrounding body text remains in the normal proportional face.
